00:59:14,420 --> 00:59:16,440
Gratefulness is the measure of our aliveness.

478
00:59:16,900 --> 00:59:21,940
Are we not dead to whatever we take for granted? Surely to be numb is to be dead.

479
00:59:23,880 --> 00:59:24,920
Think about this.

480
00:59:25,520 --> 00:59:31,500
So Irvin Yalom, Stanford psychiatrist, did a lot of research on terminally ill patients.

481
00:59:31,500 --> 00:59:39,640
He went to people who had three months, six months, up to a year to live and researched this population.

482
00:59:39,800 --> 00:59:50,920
And what he found time and again is that these people time and again were saying something to the effect of, for the first time in my life, I feel that I'm alive.

483
00:59:51,860 --> 00:59:55,420
For the first time in my life, I feel that I'm alive.

484
00:59:56,600 --> 01:00:00,300
Why? Because for the first time, I appreciate breathing.

485
01:00:00,300 --> 01:00:17,670
For the first time in many years, I appreciate my husband, my wife, my friend, my children, a flower, the grass, a conversation.

486
01:00:18,950 --> 01:00:22,370
For the first time of my life, I appreciate it.

487
01:00:22,750 --> 01:00:26,070
Whereas before, the focus was just not there.

488
01:00:26,450 --> 01:00:31,150
It was on other things, on the difficulties and the hardships and mostly on the negative.

489
01:00:31,540 --> 01:00:36,230
And remember, as far as you're concerned, the children on the bus did not exist.

